                <pb facs="0455" n="275" sameAs="frus:frus1945Berlinv02/pg275"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#small-caps">Editor’s Note</hi></head>
                <p>—At an informal meeting of the Foreign Ministers held at 4 p.m. on July 23,
                        Byrnes stated that he had expressed
                    the views of the United States on the subject of reparations from Germany to
                        Molotov at their meeting on the
                    morning of July 23 and that he had subsequently informed Eden of this talk (see <ref target="#pg295"><hi
                            rendition="#italic">post</hi>, page 295</ref>). No other record of this
                        Byrnes–Eden conversation has been found.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
